; A table (map) whose KEY is a composite type — here an array (`[+ uint]`). Under
; --preserve-encodings the deserialize loop inserts the key value into the key-encoding map and then
; again into the value-encoding map; a composite key is a `Vec<u64>` (not Copy), so the second insert
; must `.clone()` the key rather than move it. The gating predicate is the key VALUE's copy-ness
; (`is_copy`), not its ENCODING var's copy-ness (an array's encoding var refers to the length encoding
; and is always Copy) — pinning the fix for a preserve-only E0382 the default profile can't see (the
; default loop has no encoding maps, so the key is moved exactly once). The `*` occurrence is
; deliberate: a no-occurrence `{ [+ uint] => uint }` is spec-exactly-once and is rejected gracefully
; at generation (exactly-once widening — pinned by no_occurrence_arrow_map_entry_rejects_gracefully),
; and the ir-conformance oracle validates minted instances (including the empty table) against the
; spec, so the fixture spells the occurrence the generated type actually implements.
t = { * [+ uint] => uint }
; holder: embed the table so it also emits in member position.
holder = [table: t]
